# GitHub Actions Workflow Development

## Workflow Layout
Three workflows compose together:
1. **Build & Publish** (`build-and-publish.yml`) — builds and pushes the Docker image to GHCR on main
2. **Render Video** (`render-video.yml`) — manual dispatch with `composition_id` choice + per-composition string inputs
3. **Upload to Releases** (`upload-to-releases.yml`) — attaches rendered MP4 to a tagged release

## Render Video inputs
The workflow's `composition_id` input is a `type: choice` with options `HelloWorld | TransitionsDemo | CaptionsDemo`. Per-composition string inputs (title, subtitle, scene_one_text, srt_path, etc.) are all optional with sensible defaults; only the composition_id is required.

## Docker run pattern
```yaml
- name: Run video render container
  run: |
    docker run --rm \
      -v $(pwd)/output:/usr/src/app/out \
      -v $(pwd)/public:/usr/src/app/public \
      -e COMPOSITION_ID="${{ github.event.inputs.composition_id }}" \
      -e TITLE="${{ github.event.inputs.title }}" \
      -e SCENE_ONE_TEXT="${{ github.event.inputs.scene_one_text }}" \
      -e SRT_PATH="${{ github.event.inputs.srt_path }}" \
      ${{ env.REGISTRY }}/${{ env.IMAGE_NAME }}:main
```

The container reads `COMPOSITION_ID` and ignores irrelevant per-composition env vars.

## Cross-workflow artifact access
```yaml
- uses: actions/download-artifact@v4
  with:
    pattern: rendered-video-*
    merge-multiple: true
    path: ./videos
    github-token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
    run-id: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.id }}
```

The `pattern` form lets the upload-to-releases workflow collect any composition's artifact since the artifact name now includes the composition ID.

